    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325-a3">

                <pb facs="0453" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg373"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sasahe,
                        interpreter, to Mr. Lavin, immigrant
                        inspector.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seattle, Wash.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Regarding the reported loss of valuables by
                    the Japanese immigrants confined in jail last March, will state that I was
                    present with you on both occasions when you delivered the Japanese on board the
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Rosalie</hi> and the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mainlander</hi>. I then, in your company, returned their
                    money to them. At no time did they complain that they had lost any personal
                    property.</p>
                <p>In the case of the Japanese who were deported on the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mainlander</hi> to Vancouver, I will say that they were
                    taken direct from the custom-house after a conference with the secretary of the
                    Japanese consul, the manager of the Oriental Trading Company, and their
                    attorney, Mr. Fred Petersen. I was with the above-named in company of the
                    immigrants, and they made no complaint of being robbed.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Sasahe</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Japanese Interpreter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
